# 7. INTELLIGENT METADATA DISTRIBUTION ENGINE

THIS IS A CRITICAL FEATURE.

The user will provide all available information once.

The system must intelligently determine which information belongs to which platform.

Example:

The user provides:

1. Title: The Future of Artificial Intelligence
2. Description: A short explanation of AI technology.
3. Hashtags: #AI #Technology #Future
4. Tags: artificial intelligence, technology
5. Thumbnail: thumbnail.jpg
6. Privacy: Public
7. Location: Bangladesh
8. Category: Education
9. Allow comments: Yes
10. Custom notes: Publish immediately.

The application must not blindly send all 10 pieces of information to every platform.

Instead, create a metadata mapping engine.

Example:

YouTube:
- Title
- Description
- Tags
- Thumbnail
- Privacy
- Category
- Audience settings where applicable

TikTok:
- Caption assembled from relevant title and hashtags
- Video
- Privacy
- Interaction settings where supported

Instagram:
- Caption
- Hashtags
- Video
- Cover image where supported
- Location where supported

Facebook:
- Video
- Description or caption
- Thumbnail where supported
- Page destination
- Available publishing settings

The actual fields and requirements must follow each platform's current official API.

## Mapping rules

1. Detect which fields are relevant to each platform.
2. Identify required fields.
3. Identify optional fields.
4. Ignore irrelevant information.
5. Preserve the original user-provided information.
6. Do not invent missing information.
7. Do not send unsupported fields.
8. Do not silently discard user data.
9. Allow users to override automatic mapping.
10. Display a preview of the final metadata for each destination account.

## Gemini-powered metadata assistant

Integrate Gemini AI to assist with:

- Metadata classification.
- Caption formatting.
- Hashtag selection.
